                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The first game is an absolute disaster by the developers own admission.\n\nThe current game is an absolute disaster\n\nThe third game will probably be an absolute disaster if it ever exists.\n\n\n\nwhy are they talking about the third game when the second isnt even close to finished? (deadlined for december, not even happening with three wishes)\n\nwhy are they releasing the second game on top of the first games store page?\n\nwhy are they carrying on \"updating\" the first game instead of learning from it and moving on to pastures new?\n\nwhy change a game name, blaiming it on people calling it \"hands on d*ck\" when littaraly no evidence of the such exists on the store page while still haveing HoD in the title and having Hands on Deck ALLLLLLLLLLL over the store page?\n\nF*ck if i know, all i know is spend your money elsewhere. \nFind a studio who will own up to being in early access, find a team who work well together or find a quality game you atleast have a chance of enjoying. Do any of those 3 and youll be just fine.\n\n\n\nAs of writing you are paying for a VERY alpha demo of the sequal, not including the original full game as the store page states, not including the third that will probably never see the light of day but is still being advertised as if youre getting 3 games for the price one.\n\nFor an overveiw of the kind of updates to expect of this sequal please see this video (not produced by me)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nvd2ilemvWY\nthe developer would have you believe this is not what to expect because a new team is working on the second game, i however suspect this team doesnt exist and is being used as a way of convincing people that this version will be improved but that is purely speculation based on what i have seen so far.\n\nTLDR\nWarning, you may not get a complete game at all from this perchase, this should be released under early access.",
